// Design 268 sharpened design 99's position contract: an interpolation's
// column is the column of its own `{` in the SOURCE, so escapes ahead of it no
// longer shift the report. The lexer records the brace's real position now,
// where the parser used to count characters of the DECODED value — one
// character per escape — and document its columns as approximate.
//
// `\t` and `\\` each cost two source columns and one decoded character, and the
// decoded `\n` used to send the old arithmetic down its multi-line branch and
// report the error a line too far down.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: cannot interpolate value of type `Blob`
// The `{` sits at column 26 and the expression at 27; the old arithmetic said
// 18:4 — a line down and 23 columns left.
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: interp_error_position_after_escape.saw:19:27
struct Blob { n: Int }

func main() {
    let b = Blob(n: 1)
    print("a\tb\\c\{d\ne {b}")
}
